coolscan3: Initial working support for the Nikon Super Coolscan LS-5000 ED (16-bit RGB and RGBI/infrared scanning; firmware 1.03 previously rejected commands carrying an uninitialized parameter block). RGB multi-sampling and autofocus were verified. Frame selection was verified on a modified SA-21 operating as SA-30; this does not establish support for stock SA-21 or other feeders. The firmware supports a packed mode with four independent RGB samples and one aligned infrared plane, but this backend does not decode that layout and rejects the combined option before device I/O. The captured stream does not establish whether firmware combines several infrared readings internally. Firmware 1.03 rejects the tested 8-bit path.
